      "excerpt": "Board of Directors - Communitech Skip to content Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Careers Partner with us Show Site menu Close Site menu Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Meet Our Experts Careers Partner with us Join the Community Connect with us Leadership and Board of Directors At Communitech, you'll work alongside people committed to helping Waterloo Region tech companies start, scale and stay here. We bring founders, leaders and teams together, help companies move forward and amplify the people and companies building what's next. Senior Leadership Sheldon McCormick Chief Executive Officer LinkedIn Jennifer Gruber Chief Financial Officer LinkedIn Board of Directors The people who help guide Communitech are experienced founders, operators and executives who understand what building in Waterloo Region really looks like. Peter Barr Chief Strategy Officer, AltaML LinkedIn Adam Belsher CEO, Magnet Forensics LinkedIn Ruth Casselman CEO, Accelerator Centre LinkedIn Michael Doughty President & CEO, Manulife Canada (Retired) Board Chair, Communitech LinkedIn Catherine Graham CEO of commonsku Former Board Chair, Communitech LinkedIn Hongwei Liu Founder & CEO, Mappedin LinkedIn Andrew MacLeod President & CEO, Postmedia Network Inc LinkedIn Brandon Nussey CFO, Coveo LinkedIn Christopher Runstedler General Counsel &"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-ded88bd469",
      "url": "https://www.communitech.ca/about/careers.html",
      "page": "details",
      "excerpt": "Careers - Communitech Skip to content Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Careers Partner with us Show Site menu Close Site menu Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Meet Our Experts Careers Partner with us Join the Community Connect with us Working at Communitech So, what’s it like to be part of the Communitech team? As a team, our focus is great customer service and helping tech-driven companies overcome barriers to success. We stand behind our mission of 25+ years and execute it with passion, persistence and care. It's pulling together We work hard and we work together. We work to solve problems as a collective that companies face individually. We aren’t afraid to roll up our sleeves and tackle the tough stuff; and we do it free of ego, all pulling together toward our mission. It's personal well-being We’re given the tools to lead healthy and balanced lives. From competitive benefits and insurance coverage, fitness allowance and professional development funds, our hard work is balanced with a high regard for workplace happiness and personal wellbeing. It's fair, flexible compensation We have incredible benefits with no wait period. Already have benefits? Invest the spend into your RRSP! On top of respected, paid vacation we also enjoy a paid holiday shutdown. Access to an education spend allows you to choose your path"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-4987dabd66",
      "url": "https://www.communitech.ca/about/our-story.html",
      "page": "details",
      "excerpt": "Our Story - Communitech Skip to content Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Careers Partner with us Show Site menu Close Site menu Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Meet Our Experts Careers Partner with us Join the Community Connect with us COMMUNITECH Waterloo Region’s tech community since 1997. Helping Waterloo Region tech companies start, scale and stay here. 1164 Members (as of FY26) 104 Events hosted (as of FY26) $400,782,429 CAD Capital raised (as of FY26) 23 Peer Groups (as of FY26) 28 Years in business 916 AI Adoption Hours (as of FY26) Who we are Communitech is a membership organization shaped by the people building tech companies in Waterloo Region. Since 1997, we've brought founders, leaders and teams together to help more companies start here, scale here and stay here. We're working toward a stronger Waterloo Region tech community, one with more founders, more growing companies and more reasons for talented people to build their careers here. A place where companies choose to stay and others choose to put down roots. Today, more than 1,100 companies are part of the Communitech network. What we do We bring Waterloo Region tech together. Through programs, events and membership, founders, leaders and the people working across local tech companies come together to learn from one another, share what’s working"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-5ccfcfa256",
      "url": "https://www.communitech.ca/about/policies/",
      "page": "details",
      "excerpt": "Policies - Communitech Skip to content Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Careers Partner with us Show Site menu Close Site menu Events Programs Membership Pro Squad About Us Our Story Our Team Meet Our Experts Careers Partner with us Join the Community Connect with us Policies We’re all about having fun at Communitech, but we do it responsibly. We adhere to policies and procedures that ensure the protection of our team, our customers and our partners. Accessibility Communitech aims to provide a barrier-free environment for anyone who accesses our information. Accessibility Policy Multi-Year Accessibility Plan Collaboration It’s important to us that everyone’s interests are protected when collaborating. Collaboration policy Guest Wifi Acceptable Use Policy We provide free public access to all Communitech visitors. You can use the Service (don’t worry, it’s free), but only if you agree to our terms of service each time you connect! Wifi policy Privacy Communitech is committed to protecting your personal information, which is exactly why we created this policy. Privacy policy Founder Services Terms of Service In order to provide you with programming and advisory services, there are various pieces of information that we’ll need from you. These requests help us to improve our service and promote the strength of the tech ecosystem. Terms of Service"
